{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to her.</b> Through an agent. And some say it is Abraham, who was still alive. 'And He said to her' and not to him — therefore he did not suspect that Esau would be wicked." "<b>Two nations in your womb.</b> Do not be distressed if the burden of your pregnancy is great, for it is because <b>two nations are in your womb</b>, and the burden of pregnancy of two is greater than that of one." "<b>גיים.</b> It is written גוים (without yod); it is read גויים (with yod)." "<b>From your womb they shall separate.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory: this one to his righteousness and this one to his wickedness. And it was not yet known who is wicked and who is righteous; but once they grew — 'Esau was a man knowing hunting, and Jacob a whole man, dwelling in tents'." "<b>And the elder shall serve the younger.</b> Here it was decreed upon Jacob that he would be master over his brother. Rav Huna said: if Jacob is worthy — 'the elder shall serve the younger'; and if not — 'the elder, those younger than him shall serve'. Another interpretation: the many shall serve the younger."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The reverent abbreviation ה׳ expanded as YHWH per the voice rules for full divine names; the text writes the reverent form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:55.288764675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}